task: dataflow-direction
agent: opus-dataflow
started: 2026-09-11
branch: feature/dataflow-direction
worktree: ../okay-wt-ddir1
spec: specs/dataflow.md (stages 11-13), specs/federation.md (new)

why: the operator asked what is left and what is worth building, in
  the wider frame of databases and distribution, for a serious and
  for a small independent business. The answer exists only in a chat.
  A direction that lives in a chat is not a direction.

what: the answer as specs with falsifiable claims and boxes that say
  which can be checked on ONE machine — which is all there is — and
  which need machines that do not exist yet.

  dataflow stages 11-13: the log as the source (partitions that SEEK
  by epoch, so recovery is O(elements since the last epoch) and the
  output offset commits with the epoch); real network (blocked on
  machines, boxes written so the day they exist the work is a run);
  rescale at an epoch boundary.

  specs/federation.md: the one property the engine already has and
  has not been named as a product — accumulators cross, records do
  not — as the basis of aggregation across parties, with the trust
  boundary named as the work rather than waved at.

  And the small-business story as a backlog lane: one process, one
  log, one report, one page, one backup that leaves the machine.

predict: no code. The risk is writing a wish list; every box either
  names the test or names the machine it is waiting for.
